e4 = {title: "Operation Barbarossa", timestamp: "22 Jun 1941", description: "Germany invades the Soviet Union along a vast front.", status: "done"}
e5 = {title: "Attack on Pearl Harbor", timestamp: "7 Dec 1941", description: "Japan strikes the US Pacific Fleet; the United States enters the war.", status: "done"}
e6 = {title: "Battle of Midway", timestamp: "Jun 1942", description: "US Navy cripples the Japanese carrier force; the Pacific tide turns.", status: "done"}
e7 = {title: "Battle of Stalingrad", timestamp: "Aug 1942 – Feb 1943", description: "Soviet victory destroys an entire German army — the turning point in Europe.", status: "done"}
e8 = {title: "El Alamein", timestamp: "Nov 1942", description: "British victory in North Africa begins the Axis retreat there.", status: "done"}
e9 = {title: "Casablanca Conference", timestamp: "Jan 1943", description: "Allies agree on unconditional surrender and the invasion of Sicily.", status: "done"}
e10 = {title: "Invasion of Sicily and Italy", timestamp: "Jul–Sep 1943", description: "Mussolini falls; Italy surrenders, then Germany occupies the north.", status: "done"}
e11 = {title: "D-Day — Normandy landings", timestamp: "6 Jun 1944", description: "The Western Allies open a second front in northern France.", status: "done"}
e12 = {title: "Operation Bagration", timestamp: "Jun–Aug 1944", description: "Soviet offensive collapses Army Group Centre and reaches the Vistula.", status: "done"}
e13 = {title: "Liberation of Paris", timestamp: "25 Aug 1944", description: "Allied and Free French forces enter the city.", status: "done"}
e14 = {title: "Battle of the Bulge", timestamp: "Dec 1944 – Jan 1945", description: "Germany's last major counteroffensive in the west fails.", status: "done"}
e15 = {title: "Yalta Conference", timestamp: "Feb 1945", description: "Roosevelt, Churchill and Stalin plan the post-war order.", status: "done"}
e16 = {title: "Fall of Berlin", timestamp: "Apr–May 1945", description: "Soviet forces take the city; Hitler's suicide; Germany surrenders on 8 May.", status: "done"}
e17 = {title: "Hiroshima and Nagasaki", timestamp: "6 and 9 Aug 1945", description: "Atomic bombs are dropped; Japan announces surrender on 15 August.", status: "done"}
e18 = {title: "Formal Japanese surrender", timestamp: "2 Sep 1945", description: "Signed aboard USS Missouri in Tokyo Bay — the war ends.", status: "done"}
:::

The three decisive military shifts were Stalingrad and El Alamein (late 1942) in Europe and Midway (mid-1942) in the Pacific; D-Day in 1944 then turned the advantage in the west into an advance on Germany.

Note that some dates bracket long campaigns rather than single days — the war's "events" are often months-long operations. If you'd like, I can split this into European and Pacific theatres, or show casualties and costs per event.

